      },
      "body": "The alternative would be to make the narrowing explicit:\n```cpp\nsize_t operator()(const Txid& id) const noexcept\n{\n    return static_cast<size_t>(m_hasher.Hash(id.ToUint256()));\n}\n```\nbut that would just add noise for a conversion that only narrows on [platforms we want to sunset](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/32375), right?\n\n---\n\nIt has always bothered me, though, that these suppressions do not explain why they are safe.\nCould we add a short comment here?\n\n```suggestion\n# Standard unordered containers require size_t hashes, truncating the 64-bit SipHash result on 32-bit platforms\nimplicit-unsigned-integer-truncation:SaltedCoinsCacheHasher::operator()\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-07-22T18:59:06Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-22T19:13:07Z",
